<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-4697] Zeppelin Quartz scheduler checks for updates against external endpoint</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-4697</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Zeppelin uses the Quartz scheduler which has a built in update checker. This reaches out to a Terracotta server to check for updates. This should be disabled since it isn&apos;t useful and leaks information to a remote server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is recommended to be disabled in the documentation as well:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.quartz-scheduler.org/documentation/2.4.0-SNAPSHOT/best-practices.html#skip-update-check&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://www.quartz-scheduler.org/documentation/2.4.0-SNAPSHOT/best-practices.html#skip-update-check&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
